Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: node-multilang
Architecture: all
Depends: nodejs (>= 18), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Reusable multi-language string storage library (Node.js source)
 Provides retrieveData, insertData, and dbConnector for storing and
 retrieving translated strings, keyed by string_id + BCP 47 language_id,
 against SQLite, PostgreSQL, or MySQL/MariaDB.
 .
 Ships as source under /usr/lib/node_modules/multilang/ -- a plain
 require()-able package, not a full npm registry mirror. This package
 deliberately declares no Depends/Recommends on the database driver
 packages (better-sqlite3, mysql2, pg): they're native-addon/npm-registry
 packages, not reliably available as system packages with a stable name
 across distros, so install whichever backend you need via `npm install`
 alongside this package rather than expecting apt to provide it.
